Okay, so the researcher's request for this turn is: scoping inspection + high-level approach outline + assumptions/open questions, and then end_researcher_turn with stage=plan. The current stage is plan, so I should present a plan (not the full design) with assumptions and uncertainties, and wait for approval.

The task references topics: neurips2024/97431/11:setup_17 and setup_18 — probably paper-derived setup topics. I don't have access to those documents. The brief mentions AutoDAN (token-level, Liu et al. 2023, genetic-algorithm-based generation of human-readable jailbreak prompts — actually AutoDAN is "Automatic Generation of Jailbreak Prompts", token-level/fluency-constrained genetic algorithm over prompt suffix tokens) and PAIR (Choudhary et al. 2023, attacker-LLM iteratively refines prompt, black-box, ~20 iterations, transfer attack). Question about 2x2 structure: attack style (AutoDAN vs PAIR) × attacker strength × defense strength × previously-tested tricks (attack memory). This resembles a combination of "Jailbreak in the Wild"/"Bag of Tricks"/"OIB (Orchestral-In-the-attack)?" — actually the "previously tested tricks" axis could be "transfer learning/attack memory", or might refer to "TAP with priors"? Or to NeurIPS 2024 paper 97431… I can't verify the source; should flag that topics setup_17/setup_18 aren't available in the workspace, and ask the researcher to provide them or confirm parameters.

ASR definition: standard = fraction of harmful behaviors (e.g., 100 AdvBench "how-to" behaviors / StrongREJECT) for which the attack finds at least one successful jailbreak within the query budget. Judged by keyword/rule matching (AutoDAN/HarmBench style: match against forbidden keywords), or by an attacker-model classifier (PAIR uses an NLI-based judge scoring semantic agreement + harmfulness), or LLM-judge (e.g., GPT-4 judge / StrongREJECT rubric).

Attacker strength: operationalized as query budget (number of target-model queries / iterations), number of parallel branches, and white-box access level (none / logprob access / open weights for GCG-style init). Levels: low/medium/high.

Defense strength: none (vanilla aligned model) / prompt-level filtering (perplexity filter, random-perturbation baseline; prompt classifier e.g. a llama-guard-style classifier or self-reminders) / stronger composed defenses (safe-completion, RLHF checkpoint / fine-tuned defense like NeMo-style guard + safe-completion). Levels: none/weak/strong.

Previously tested tricks (attack memory): maintain a persistent library of successfully jailbroken suffixes/pairs from prior runs, and warm-start the attacker from it (transfer/warm-start), versus cold-start. Two candidate meanings — researcher needs to confirm which.

Design: full factorial 2 (attack style) × 3 (attacker strength) × 3 (defense strength) × 2 (memory) = 36 cells, behaviors N=100 (AdvBench subset) + StrongREJECT held-out; per-cell ASR; primary analysis: mixed-effects logistic regression at the response level, or aggregated proportion tests; interaction terms attacker×defense and attack-style×memory. Because of design only + no compute resources: specify the harness to be built, deliverables, and feasibility check (dry-run of scoring pipeline on synthetic outputs).

Flag as unknowns: source topics setup_17/18 unavailable; the paper artifacts don't state hyperparameters; no datasets; no judge model.

Also, note that task.json's documents/track.md says "Design-only task; repository and compute resources are not required."

