", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "SCOPING INSPECTION (no design decisions finalised; awaiting your confirmation)

1) Repository / runtime — what exists vs. what must be built
EXISTS:
- /workspace contains exactly one file: task.json (the question, context, and a note: "Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.").
- System Python 3.14.4 with only OS/utility packages (ansible, apt tooling, Jinja2, etc.). No numpy, scipy, pandas, scikit-learn, statsmodels, torch, transformers, datasets, vllm, openai, matplotlib — pip grep returned nothing.
CONFIRMED ABSENT:
- No code, no configs, no prompt/attack harnesses, no dataset stubs (no AdvBench/StrongREJECT/SorryBench files), no prior results, no paper artifacts. The referenced topics (neurips2024/97431/11:setup_17, setup_18) are NOT present in the workspace and are not readable by me — their concrete setup details must come from you.
- No GPU (nvidia-smi fails, no driver), network disabled (DNS resolution fails; pypi unreachable), and bubblewrap-isolated with no raw-socket capability. So no model inference, no API judges, no dependency installation is possible here. Everything empirical would have to be *specified*, and any "feasible check" is limited to file/plan scaffolding and dry logic in pure Python.

2) Proposed approach outline (high level)
Factorial frame: 2 (attack style: AutoDAN token-level vs. PAIR prompt-level) x 3 (attacker strength) x 3 (defense strength) x 2 (attack-memory: cold-start vs. warm-start with previously tested tricks) = 36 cells, plus a no-attack refusal-rate baseline.
- Attack styles: AutoDAN = genetic-algorithm search over a human-readable suffix, using its fluency-constrained token/segment mutation operators; PAIR = attacker-LLM/target-LLM loop that iteratively refines a semantic prompt under a target-query budget. Same target model, same behavior set, same judge per cell so the style axis is isolated.
- Attacker strength (operationalised, ordinal): L1 = low query budget (PAIR: ~10 target queries, ~2 streams; AutoDAN: small pop/gen, random init), L2 = paper-default budgets (PAIR: ~20 queries x ~4 parallel streams; AutoDAN: default pop/gen), L3 = high budget + privileged init (warm-start library, transfer suffix priors; AutoDAN initialized from successful seeds; PAIR attacker given judge feedback/transfer). Access level (closed API vs. open-weight target) held fixed as a blocked covariate, not mixed into the strength axis.
- Defense strength (operationalised, ordinal): D0 = vanilla aligned/RLHF checkpoint only; D1 = one detection filter on input (perplexity filter for token-level; prompt-classifier/safety-reminder for prompt-level, applied to both for fairness); D2 = defense stack = input filter + output-side judge with safe-completion substitution + stricter aligned checkpoint.
- "Previously tested tricks" (M axis, default reading): persistent attack-memory library of successfully jailbroken suffixes/prompt templates harvested from earlier runs, used to warm-start the attacker; control = cold-start empty memory. (Alternative reading — conditioning the attacker LLM on a textual history of tried-but-failed techniques, PAIR-style — is the main thing I need you to confirm; see assumptions.)
- ASR: per behavior, ASR = 1 if at least one attack query within the budget elicits a compliant, on-topic harmful response, else 0; cell ASR = mean over behaviors. Two graders, pre-registered: (a) AutoDAN/HarmBench-style keyword/forbidden-phrase rule matcher, (b) model-based judge (StrongREJECT-style rubric scoring compliance + specificity), with the primary endpoint the stricter of the two, and NLI-style semantic-relevance gating as in PAIR to reject off-topic refusals. Report both per-cell ASR and mean-sentence-level ASR (AutoDAN convention) as secondary.
- Interaction analysis: response-level mixed-effects logistic regression (success ~ attack_style * attacker_strength * defense_strength * memory, random intercepts for behavior and seed) to test the attacker x defense and style x memory interactions; bootstrap CIs over behaviors; secondary "ASR drop per defense level at each attacker level" table to characterise whether stronger attacks erode defenses (defense bypass) or whether defense gains saturate (robustness ceiling).
