Matrix inversion (k×k, general):

def inv(M):
    n=len(M); A=[row[:]+[1.0 if i==j else 0.0 for j in range(n)] for i,row in enumerate(M)]
    for c in range(n):
        # pivot
        p=max(range(c,n), key=lambda r: abs(A[r][c]))
        if abs(A[p][c])<1e-12: raise ZeroDivisionError
        A[c],A[p]=A[p],A[c]
        pv=A[c][c]
        A[c]=[x/pv for x in A[c]]
        for r in range(n):
            if r!=c:
                f=A[r][c]
                if f: A[r]=[a-f*b for a,b in zip(A[r],A[c])]
    return [row[n:] for row in A]

IRLS:
X: list of rows length k; y 0/1.
beta=[0]*k
for it in range(50):
    p=[sig(dot(beta,x)) for x in X] clamped to [1e-9,1-1e-9]
    w=[p_*(1-p_) ...]
    z=[eta + (y-p_)/w_]
    XtWX[i][j]=Σ w x_i x_j; XtWz[i]=Σ w z x_i
    beta_new = inv(XtWX) @ XtWz; converge on small delta.

Sandwich: XtWX (same), meat = Σ_c g g^T where g = Σ_{i in c} x_i*(y_i-p_i). var = bread meat bread. se_ad = sqrt(var[ad][ad]).

Design columns: intercept, xa, xd, xa*xd.

